2	// the app's sources (`mac/Sources/`) for the APIs that write audio data to
3	// disk. It matches API tokens, not file extensions, so a comment or a string
4	// literal mentioning "audio file" stays legal while an actual writer does not.
5	//
6	// This is the v1 state (docs/DESIGN-AND-TRADEOFFS.md §6: "in v1, not stored at
7	// all"). The roadmap's v3 deliberately adds a rolling audio buffer for
8	// retraining — landing that is a product decision, not an incidental line of
9	// Swift, so it updates this pack (and the mic prompt) in the same PR that
10	// removes or narrows this check, exactly as no-network-client expects of a
11	// deliberate future egress decision.
12	//
13	// Dependency-free by design (a local pack must load without the canon mount),
14	// so the finding object is built by hand rather than via the engine helper.
